{#
  A body's mark as an image, never larger than `cap` pixels on its longer side, whatever the format (Nathan,
  4 October 2026: "Cap marks by display size, not by file type. Same maximum for every format: 600 on the
  record, 400 on /organizations, 200 on /schools"). An SVG has no size of its own and grows to fill its box,
  so it gets width and height scaled to the cap and a CSS max-width; a raster file is served as a copy no
  larger than the cap (the file as handed over stays the archive copy) and capped the same way.

    mark   the asset
    cap    the longest side, in pixels
    style  optional extra CSS
    lazy   optional, load lazily
#}
{%- set w = mark.width ?: cap -%}{%- set h = mark.height ?: cap -%}
{%- set k = min(1, cap / max(w, h)) -%}
{%- set dw = (w * k)|round -%}{%- set dh = (h * k)|round -%}
{%- set tr = mark.extension|lower == 'svg' ? null : { width: cap, height: cap, mode: 'fit', upscale: false } -%}
<img src="{{ mark.getUrl(tr) }}" alt="{{ mark.alt ?: mark.title }}" width="{{ dw }}" height="{{ dh }}" style="max-width:min(100%, {{ dw }}px);max-height:{{ dh }}px;height:auto;{{ style ?? '' }}"{% if lazy ?? false %} loading="lazy"{% endif %}>
